 nutritional parameters.", "CÁPSULA ENDOSCÓPICA:La cápsula endoscópica visualiza linfangiectasias y edema en el yeyuno proximal, proporcionando información adicional sobre la condición del paciente.", "ATROFIA ÓPTICA:La atrofia óptica es un hallazgo observado en el fondo de ojo del paciente, indicando daño severo en la vía visual.", "DEBILIDAD PROGRESIVA:La debilidad progresiva es un síntoma que se presenta a los 16 años, afectando principalmente a los miembros inferiores y superiores.", "HIPOGLICEMIAS:Las hipoglucemias son episodios que ocurren debido a la suspensión irregular del tratamiento antidiabético, afectando la salud del paciente.", "SENSACIÓN DE PLENITUD POSTPRANDIAL:La sensación de plenitud postprandial es un síntoma que el paciente experimenta después de las comidas, indicando problemas digestivos.", "IMAGEN DE RMN:La imagen de resonancia magnética nuclear (RMN) muestra cambios en la sustancia blanca del cerebro, lo que es relevante para el diagnóstico del paciente.", "PATOLOGÍAS:PATOLOGÍAS refer to diseases or disorders that can impact carbohydrate digestion and absorption. These health conditions necessitate nutritional support and dietary management, especially concerning FODMAP intake.", "TYMP:The TYMP gene is located on chromosome 22q13.33 and encodes a protein involved in the phosphorylation of thymidine, mutations in which cause MNGIE.", "GARONE:Garone is a researcher who reviewed 102 cases of MNGIE between 1988 and 2011, contributing to the understanding of the syndrome.", "TIMIDINA:Thymidine is a nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE due to the deficiency of thymidine phosphorylase.", "DEOXIURIDINA:Deoxyuridine is another nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE, indicating a metabolic disturbance.", "NEUROLOGICAL SYMPTOMS:Neurological symptoms associated with MNGIE include peripheral neuropathy, ptosis, ophthalmoplegia, and leukoencephalopathy.", "DIGESTIVE SYMPTOMS:Digestive symptoms of MNGIE include gastrointestinal dysmotility, early satiety, nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain.", "ANALYTICAL FINDINGS:Analytical findings in MNGIE include elevated levels of thymidine and deoxyuridine in plasma, which are characteristic of the disorder.", "NEUROIMAGING FINDINGS:Neuroimaging findings in MNGIE typically show diffuse alterations in white matter, indicative of leukoencephalopathy."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}